# A1/A1.1/A1_03_numbers_and_personal_info.letz
# Source: Quizlet "A1 Basics Beginner Luxembourgish Lesson 3"
#   https://quizlet.com/_h2t12h
# Slash variants and bracket alternatives split into atomic pairs;
# (m)/(f)/(pl) markers stripped; (formal)/(informal) qualifiers stripped;
# (were) and (boyfriend) bracket alternatives produce extra @en variants.
# @fill added: question words (Wéi/Wéini/Wou), hunn vs sinn in personal-info
# frames, kee/keng negation contrast, numbers, and prepositions (zu/um/bei/an).

@lesson A1.03 "Numbers & Personal Info"

# --- Numbers (Quizlet cards 1-11) ---
@word null = zero
@word eent = one
@word zwee = two
@word dräi = three
@word véier = four
@word fënnef = five
@word sechs = six
@word siwen = seven
@word aacht = eight
@word néng = nine
@word zéng = ten

# --- Phrase / vocabulary (Quizlet card 29) ---
@word zesummen = together

# --- Family nouns (Quizlet cards 30-31) ---
@word de Brudder = brother
@word Bridder = brothers

@word d'Schwëster = sister
@word Schwësteren = sisters

# --- Vocabulary from sentences (coverage backfill) ---
@word d'Telefonsnummer = telephone number
@word d'Joer = year
@word de Gebuertsdag = birthday
@word fannen = to find

# --- Sentences (Quizlet cards 12-28, 32-39) ---

@sentence
@lu Wéi ass deng Telefonsnummer?
@lu Wéi ass Är Telefonsnummer?
@en What is your telephone number?
@distractor-en together
@distractor-en zero
@distractor-en one
@distractor-lu zesummen
@distractor-lu null
@distractor-lu eent

@sentence
@lu Meng Telefonsnummer ass...
@en My phone number is...
@distractor-en three
@distractor-en four
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-lu véier

@sentence
@lu Wou wunnt Dir?
@lu Wou wunns du?
@en Where do you live?
@distractor-en five
@distractor-en six
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-en when
@distractor-lu fënnef
@distractor-lu sechs
@distractor-lu siwen
@distractor-lu Wéini

@sentence
@lu Ech wunnen an der Belsch, zu Bréissel.
@en I live in Belgium, in Brussels.
@distractor-en nine
@distractor-en ten
@distractor-lu néng
@distractor-lu zéng

@sentence
@lu Ech wunnen um Kierchbierg.
@en I live in the Kirchberg neighbourhood.
@distractor-en together
@distractor-en zero
@distractor-lu zesummen
@distractor-lu null

@sentence
@lu Wéi vill Joer hutt Dir?
@lu Wéi vill Joer hues du?
@en How many years do you have?
@distractor-en one
@distractor-en two
@distractor-en three
@distractor-lu eent
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-lu dräi

@sentence
@lu Wéini ass Äre Gebuertsdag?
@lu Wéini ass däi Gebuertsdag?
@en When is your birthday?
@distractor-en five
@distractor-en six
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu fënnef
@distractor-lu sechs
@distractor-lu siwen
@distractor-lu Wou

@sentence
@lu Wéini sidd Dir gebuer?
@lu Wéini bass du gebuer?
@en When were you born?
@distractor-en nine
@distractor-en ten
@distractor-en together
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu néng
@distractor-lu zéng
@distractor-lu zesummen
@distractor-lu Wou

@sentence
@lu Mir si bestuet.
@en We are married.
@distractor-en sister
@distractor-en brother
@distractor-lu Schwëster
@distractor-lu Brudder

@sentence
@lu Ech si gescheet.
@en I'm divorced.
@distractor-en together
@distractor-en one
@distractor-lu zesummen
@distractor-lu eent

@sentence
@lu Mir hunn eis getrennt.
@en We separated.
@distractor-en two
@distractor-en three
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-lu dräi

@sentence
@lu Ech fannen dech léif.
@en I like you.
@distractor-en four
@distractor-en five
@distractor-lu véier
@distractor-lu fënnef

@sentence
@lu Ech hu Kanner.
@en I have children.
@distractor-en sister
@distractor-en brother
@distractor-lu Schwëster
@distractor-lu Brudder

@sentence
@lu Ech hu keng Kanner.
@en I don't have children.
@distractor-en six
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-lu sechs
@distractor-lu siwen

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn e Frënd.
@en I have a friend.
@en I have a boyfriend.
@distractor-en eight
@distractor-en nine
@distractor-lu aacht
@distractor-lu néng

@sentence
@lu Ech hu kee Frënd.
@en I do not have a friend.
@en I do not have a boyfriend.
@distractor-en ten
@distractor-en together
@distractor-lu zéng
@distractor-lu zesummen

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn eng Frëndin.
@en I have a girlfriend.
@distractor-en zero
@distractor-en one
@distractor-lu null
@distractor-lu eent

@sentence
@lu Ech hu keng Frëndin.
@en I do not have a girlfriend.
@distractor-en two
@distractor-en three
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-lu dräi

@sentence
@lu Ech gi bei mäi Mann.
@en I'm going to my husband.
@distractor-en four
@distractor-en five
@distractor-lu véier
@distractor-lu fënnef

@sentence
@lu Ech ginn net bei mäi Mann.
@en I'm not going to my husband.
@distractor-en six
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-lu sechs
@distractor-lu siwen

# --- @fill: question words -------------------------------------------------------
# Wéi/Wéini/Wou confusion is a genuine A1 pain point. Blanks are
# sentence-initial so no Eifeler Regel risk; distractors are the
# other question words from A1.02.

@fill
@lu [Wéi] ass deng Telefonsnummer, wannechgelift?
@en [What] is your telephone number, please?
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-en Where
@distractor-en When
@distractor-en How

@fill
@lu [Wéini] bass du gebuer, wannechgelift?
@en [When] were you born, please?
@distractor-lu Wéi
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-en How
@distractor-en Where
@distractor-en What

@fill
@lu [Wou] wunnt deng Schwëster?
@en [Where] does your sister live?
@distractor-lu Wéi
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-en How
@distractor-en When
@distractor-en What

# --- @fill: hunn vs sinn (personal-info frames) ---------------------------------
# The learner confuses hunn (possession) and sinn (state/identity) in
# personal-info contexts. Distractors are the wrong auxiliary.

@fill
@lu Ech [si] bestuet a frou.
@en I [am] married and happy.
@distractor-lu hunn
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu gees
@distractor-en have
@distractor-en give
@distractor-en go

@fill
@lu Ech [hunn] zwee Bridder a véier Kanner.
@en I [have] two brothers and four children.
@distractor-lu sinn
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu kommen
@distractor-en am
@distractor-en give
@distractor-en come

@fill
@lu Ech [si] gescheet, mee ech sinn net traureg.
@en I [am] divorced, but I'm not sad.
@distractor-lu hunn
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu kréien
@distractor-en have
@distractor-en give
@distractor-en get

# --- @fill: kee/keng negation contrast ------------------------------------------
# kee (masc.) vs keng (fem.) is a genuine confusion point. Distractors
# are the wrong gender form plus a non-negation word.

@fill
@lu Ech hu [kee] Brudder, mee dräi Schwësteren.
@en I have [no] brother, but three sisters.
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu eent
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-en a
@distractor-en one
@distractor-en three

@fill
@lu Ech hu [keng] Schwëster, mee zwee Bridder.
@en I have [no] sister, but two brothers.
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu eent
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-en a
@distractor-en one
@distractor-en two

# --- @fill: numbers in context ---------------------------------------------------
# The blank is the number; distractors are other numbers from this lesson.
# Frames reuse taught vocabulary (Joer, Bridder, Kanner).

@fill
@lu Ech hu [fënnef] Joer.
@en I am [five] years old.
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-lu siwen
@distractor-lu zéng
@distractor-en three
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-en ten

@fill
@lu Ech hu [sechs] Schwësteren, mir si [siwen] zesummen.
@en I have [six] sisters, we are [seven] together.
@distractor-lu aacht
@distractor-lu véier
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-en eight
@distractor-en four
@distractor-en three

# --- @fill: prepositions (zu/um/bei/an) -----------------------------------------
# Prepositions from sentences this lesson and A1.01 teach. Determiners
# stay in the frame so correct text is tile-independent.

@fill
@lu Meng Schwëster wunnt [zu] Bréissel.
@en My sister lives [in] Brussels.
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu um
@distractor-lu aus
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en on
@distractor-en from

@fill
@lu Mäi Brudder wunnt [um] Kierchbierg.
@en My brother lives [in the] Kirchberg neighbourhood.
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-lu zu
@distractor-en at the
@distractor-en to
@distractor-en in
